  "description": "This course covers foundational web software development techniques, including HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript ES6+, and RESTful API design; client-server communication using HTTP/HTTPS protocols; front-end frameworks like React and Vue.js; database integration with MySQL and MongoDB; server-side development using Node.js and Express.js; version control with Git and GitHub; and security best practices such as XSS and CSRF mitigation. Topics include DOM manipulation, AJAX requests, JSON data handling, and responsive design principles. The course also introduces software development lifecycle concepts and project management tools like Jira and Trello.",
